    "recoil": {
      "_comment": "AKS-74U: 5.45x39 from a short, light carbine with a booster - a quick, fairly soft shove back into the shoulder, then the muzzle rises a beat later. Every round leaves at its own angle (kickSpread, a little right on average), with its own timing (timeJitter); the first round of a burst hits hardest. In full auto the sideways drift is a random walk (wander) that loosens as the burst goes on (burstGrowth), so it climbs up and a little right but never the same way twice. Critically damped smoothing: no bounce.",
